# The wire fixtures are compared byte for byte, by two implementations, against
# what each one writes. A checkout that turned their line endings into CRLF — git
# on Windows does, by default — makes every one of them a mismatch that is not a
# defect. Checked out exactly as committed, everywhere.
testdata/** -text

# gofmt writes LF and reports any file that differs from what it writes, so a
# Windows checkout with CRLF is every Go file reported unformatted.
*.go text eol=lf
